Implement user story MOCK3-1: Riders aged exactly 65 are charged the adult fare

## Story Description
The fare rules say riders aged 65 and over pay the concession fare. A rider aged exactly 65 is charged the full adult fare of 350 cents instead of 175. Riders aged 66 and above are charged correctly, so the boundary itself is wrong rather than the rule.

## Acceptance Criteria
- A rider aged exactly 65 with no pass is charged the concession fare.
- A rider aged 64 with no pass is still charged the base fare.
- The existing fare behaviour for children, pass holders and adults is unchanged.

## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.

_(fix-plan, from: code-graph-detective)_

- **src/fares.ts** (`fareFor`): This function computes the fare for a rider. The comparison `rider.age > 65` on line 10 excludes age 65 from the concession tier, causing riders aged exactly 65 to fall through to the base fare. Changing `>` to `>=` makes age 65 satisfy the condition, producing the concession fare as the rules require.  <== **THIS CHANGE PRODUCES THE VALUE** — it is what makes the new or corrected data exist. Without it, every other change here only moves a value that never changed. [runs: server]
  - **Minimal fix:** Change `rider.age > 65` to `rider.age >= 65` on line 10 of src/fares.ts. Reuse the existing constant CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS (already imported/declared in this file) ? no new helper needed.
- **test/fares.test.ts** (`fareFor`)  [NO EDIT REQUIRED — part of the fix, correctly left unchanged]: This test file exercises fareFor but does not cover age 65 (the boundary). Existing tests use ages 8, 30, and 70. After the production fix, all existing tests still pass, but age 65 remains untested. This file needs no edit (test agent owns it), only verification that existing tests continue to pass.  (verify only — no edit expected here) [runs: server]
  - **Minimal fix:** No edit required. Verify that existing tests still pass after the production change. The test suite does not yet cover age 65 ? that coverage gap is for the test agent to address separately.



